---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/company.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contact" description="Contact Chudware for account support, subscriptions, organization deployment, security disclosure, privacy, and legal questions.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h1>Send the question to the team responsible for it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Use the address that matches the request. Do not include passwords, payment-card numbers, provider credentials, or confidential project files unless support has arranged a secure transfer.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-routes">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Direct routes</p>
        <h2 id="co-routes" class="co-anchor">Contact addresses.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="co-routes">
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Sales</p>
          <h3>Plans and organization deployment</h3>
          <p>Enterprise accounts, multiple-user deployment, procurement, and commercial questions not answered on the pricing page.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20access">sales@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
          <h3>Product, account, and billing help</h3>
          <p>Sign-in or entitlement problems, a workspace that will not open, a failed workflow, or a billing issue.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:support@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20support">support@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route co-route-urgent">
          <p class="eyebrow">Security</p>
          <h3>Vulnerability disclosure</h3>
          <p>Include the affected surface, impact, and reproducible steps. Test only against accounts and data you are authorized to use. Chudware does not currently operate a bug bounty or publish a response-time commitment.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:security@chudware.com?subject=Security%20report">security@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h3>Account and service data</h3>
          <p>Access or deletion requests, hosted project data, sessions and devices, and provider connections.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:privacy@chudware.com?subject=Privacy%20request">privacy@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
          <h3>Terms and agreements</h3>
          <p>Questions about the terms of service, privacy policy, EULA, or refund policy.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:legal@chudware.com?subject=Legal%20question">legal@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
        <article class="co-route">
          <p class="eyebrow">General</p>
          <h3>Other enquiries</h3>
          <p>Use the sales address when the request does not fit one of the specialist routes.</p>
          <a class="co-route-address" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Chudware%20enquiry">sales@chudware.com</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-self">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <header class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Self-service</p>
          <h2 id="co-self" class="co-anchor">Documentation for common questions.</h2>
        </header>
        <ul class="co-selfserve">
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/faq/">FAQ</a><p>Product scope, access, platforms, files, AI providers, subscriptions, and support.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Documentation</a><p>Installation and task guides for modeling, assemblies, CAM, product data, reverse engineering, and the copilot.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/security/">Security</a><p>Gateway architecture, account controls, secret handling, disclosure, and current assurance boundaries.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/pricing/">Pricing</a><p>Trial, Desktop, Studio, education eligibility, storage, and Enterprise access.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/download/">Download</a><p>The live native release catalog and authenticated download route.</p></li>
          <li><a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Changelog</a><p>Published release and product updates.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="co-aside">
        <div class="co-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">For a useful support report</p>
          <p>Include the browser or native application, operating system, product version, steps taken, expected result, actual result, and any exact error text. For a security report, include a minimal reproduction and its impact.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate first</p>
      <h2>Use the trial on a representative workflow.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Create an account or review the product examples before contacting the team.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/gallery/">View the gallery</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
